WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:10.050
MARKUS KLUTE: Welcome
back to 8.701.

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:14.040
So in this lecture, we look
at the interaction of W bosons

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:18.810
with quarks, or the charged
weak interaction of quarks.

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:21.750
Let's just make a
number of observations.

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:24.630
Now, we observe that the weak
interaction respects the lepton

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:27.900
generation, meaning
that a W couples

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:30.480
to an electron and
an electron neutrino,

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:33.270
but not an electron
muon neutrino.

00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:37.420
But in the case of the quarks,
there is violation of this.

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:41.700
So there is a disrespect
of the quark generation

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:44.980
when it comes to the
interaction with Ws.

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:47.970
So when you investigate
these two diagrams here,

00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:54.100
you find that the W couples to
the V quark and the U quark,

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:57.330
but it also couples
to the S quark.

00:00:57.330 --> 00:01:00.960
S quark and the U
quark, all right?

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:03.724
In order to encapsulate this,
we have to make a correction.

00:01:03.724 --> 00:01:05.099
And the corrections
are typically

00:01:05.099 --> 00:01:09.660
called cosine theta C
and sine theta C. Theta

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:13.110
C is the Cabibbo angle,
so theta Cabibbo.

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:15.510
Turns out this is rather
small, so it's a decrease.

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:19.620
So it is a correction,
a small correction.

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:21.960
We studied the
partial decay width

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:26.340
of the kaon in leptonic
decays over the partial decays

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:29.520
to a pion of the pion
in leptonic decays.

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:31.200
We found that there
is a set of forms

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:33.180
that are the form factor
for the pion decay

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:35.400
and a form factor
for the kaon decay.

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:37.680
It turns out that
the form factors are

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:40.190
due to this
additional correction,

00:01:40.190 --> 00:01:43.680
so you find the tangent-square
of the Cabibbo angle

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:46.350
as part of this correction.

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:47.430
Good.

00:01:47.430 --> 00:01:48.737
So far, so good.

00:01:48.737 --> 00:01:50.070
Now we have made an observation.

00:01:50.070 --> 00:01:52.290
We haven't explained
anything yet.

00:01:52.290 --> 00:01:56.460
We can make one more
observation, or discuss one,

00:01:56.460 --> 00:02:01.560
and that's the decay of neutral
kaons to a pair of muons.

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:06.410
It turns out that those
are not very likely.

00:02:06.410 --> 00:02:11.190
Even so, you would expect that
the amplitude has a factor here

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:15.570
of sine and cosine of
Cabibbo, so the amplitude

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:19.365
should be on the order of sine
theta Cabibbo times cosine

00:02:19.365 --> 00:02:21.810
theta Cabibbo.

00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:25.170
So when this was
studied, the charm quark

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:27.660
hadn't been discovered.

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:32.340
And the explanation to why
this decay is suppressed

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:36.800
comes from the fact that there
is a second diagram here,

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:40.370
where we just replace the U
quark in this rule with a C

00:02:40.370 --> 00:02:41.240
quark.

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:47.690
This diagram contributes there's
a minus sign to the amplitude.

00:02:47.690 --> 00:02:51.140
And therefore, those two
diagrams, they cancel.

00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:51.860
Right?

00:02:51.860 --> 00:02:55.370
They are the same magnitude,
about the same magnitude,

00:02:55.370 --> 00:02:57.388
and they have an opposite sign.

00:02:57.388 --> 00:02:59.180
So this was the first
indication that there

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:01.760
must be a force
quark contributing

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:02.850
to this kind of process.

00:03:02.850 --> 00:03:04.156
That's the charm quark.

00:03:06.850 --> 00:03:09.440
Let me now try to understand
what's going on here.

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:13.420
Why is the W coupling modified?

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:17.320
Or why is not the full
down quark or charm

00:03:17.320 --> 00:03:21.340
and strange quark participating
in the weak interaction?

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:22.690
We can do the following here.

00:03:22.690 --> 00:03:28.030
We can rewrite-- we note
that the weak interaction

00:03:28.030 --> 00:03:31.370
eigenstate, the eigenstate which
participate in the [INAUDIBLE],,

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:33.177
is not the eigenstate
of the particle

00:03:33.177 --> 00:03:36.060
itself, the so-called
mass eigenstate.

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:38.750
So we have to write
the weak eigenstate

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:44.580
as the linear combination of the
mass eigenstate or [INAUDIBLE]..

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:46.620
This can be done
in this matrix form

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:52.920
here, where we simply
multiply the weak eigenstates

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:56.790
with a matrix, and just
basically rotate it

00:03:56.790 --> 00:03:59.610
into the mass eigenstate.

00:03:59.610 --> 00:04:05.100
So this was proposed by
Cabibbo, and rather successful.

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:08.400
But it didn't incorporate the
third-generation particle.

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:11.815
And this was done by
Kobayashi and Maskawa,

00:04:11.815 --> 00:04:16.800
who generalized the scheme
and proposed the so-called CKM

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:19.589
matrix, the easier
form Cabibbo--

00:04:19.589 --> 00:04:23.370
Cabibbo, Kobayashi, and Maskawa.

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:27.130
Because of constraints
we'll discuss

00:04:27.130 --> 00:04:31.740
in one of the
recitations, this matrix

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:36.720
can be parameterized as only
three independent angles

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:40.150
and one complex phase as
independent parameters.

00:04:40.150 --> 00:04:42.810
So you can choose
different parameterization

00:04:42.810 --> 00:04:46.840
to capture that there's only
four parameters in this matrix,

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:49.750
which has nine components.

00:04:49.750 --> 00:04:52.830
One is by thinking
about this matrix

00:04:52.830 --> 00:04:57.090
as three independent rotations
and this complex phase here.

00:04:57.090 --> 00:04:58.920
In terms of
numerical values, you

00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:04.060
see that the diagonal
elements of this matrix

00:05:04.060 --> 00:05:08.680
are very close to 1,
meaning that this mixing is

00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:11.210
on the block sector of
the [INAUDIBLE] effect.

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:14.455
You find that those next-nearest
off-diagonal elements are

00:05:14.455 --> 00:05:19.300
on the order of 20%, and the
next-to-next off-elements

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:22.150
are even smaller.

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:23.140
OK?

00:05:23.140 --> 00:05:24.790
This leads us, then,
to the discussion

00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:27.460
that we can use different
parameterization in order

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:29.020
to capture [INAUDIBLE].

00:05:29.020 --> 00:05:31.360
We already discussed the
standard parameterization,

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:35.500
which you can really think
about three different rotation.

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:40.210
And the values of those
angles are give here, together

00:05:40.210 --> 00:05:44.907
with the value of
this additional phase.

00:05:44.907 --> 00:05:47.240
Another way to look at this
is the so-called Wolfenstein

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:48.303
parameterization.

00:05:48.303 --> 00:05:49.720
And this captures
the fact that it

00:05:49.720 --> 00:05:53.140
seems like that there's
a correction being

00:05:53.140 --> 00:05:54.820
applied to the actual particle.

00:05:54.820 --> 00:05:58.210
So you find elements
of the order of lambda.

00:05:58.210 --> 00:06:01.390
Lambda is about 22%.

00:06:01.390 --> 00:06:04.150
And you find elements
which are in the order of 1

00:06:04.150 --> 00:06:07.210
minus the lambda-square
correction.

00:06:07.210 --> 00:06:10.290
And then there is elements which
are of lambda-square and lambda

00:06:10.290 --> 00:06:11.980
3rd power.

00:06:11.980 --> 00:06:15.610
So this captures the
matrix, and then there's

00:06:15.610 --> 00:06:18.940
higher-order corrections to
that which are of order lambda

00:06:18.940 --> 00:06:21.460
to the 4th power.

00:06:21.460 --> 00:06:21.960
OK?

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:30.660
Because there's constraints on
this matrix-- and specifically,

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:34.710
unitarity constraints, meaning
that we have three generations

00:06:34.710 --> 00:06:38.130
that will make a mixing of
those three mass eigenstates

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:43.710
to weak eigenstate-- then
unitarity, the total number

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:47.070
of particles in this
discussion, is conserved.

00:06:47.070 --> 00:06:49.560
This will change if there
would be, for example, a force

00:06:49.560 --> 00:06:51.180
generation particle.

00:06:51.180 --> 00:06:53.978
So the study of weak-charged
interaction with quarks

00:06:53.978 --> 00:06:55.770
helps us to understand
whether or not there

00:06:55.770 --> 00:06:59.160
might be a force generation.

00:06:59.160 --> 00:07:00.960
We'll not go into
too much detail here,

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:04.500
but also, the complex
phase explains

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:08.700
part of our understanding
of CP violation.

00:07:08.700 --> 00:07:12.792
And we might discuss this in a
little bit of a later lecture.

00:07:12.792 --> 00:07:14.750
But nevertheless, what
we can achieve from here

00:07:14.750 --> 00:07:22.290
is those unitarity
constraints, just simply

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:25.088
summing over the
matrix elements,

00:07:25.088 --> 00:07:27.480
the scalar product
of matrix elements.

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:31.850
And those where the
contribution vanishes,

00:07:31.850 --> 00:07:35.090
so those where j
and k are not equal,

00:07:35.090 --> 00:07:38.405
those can be represented
as a triangle.

00:07:38.405 --> 00:07:39.530
That's kind of interesting.

00:07:39.530 --> 00:07:40.820
You can just rewrite this.

00:07:40.820 --> 00:07:43.850
You just say that those
three elements of the sum

00:07:43.850 --> 00:07:45.110
are equal to 0.

00:07:45.110 --> 00:07:46.860
Then you normalize
by one element.

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:54.080
In this case here,
normalize by Vcd, Vcb.

00:07:54.080 --> 00:07:57.150
And so then this makes
this point being 0,

00:07:57.150 --> 00:07:58.940
and so we have
this nice triangle

00:07:58.940 --> 00:08:03.700
here, which has three
angles, alpha, beta,

00:08:03.700 --> 00:08:08.470
and gamma, and this
point here, rho and eta.

00:08:08.470 --> 00:08:10.630
And so this is a nice
way to illustrate

00:08:10.630 --> 00:08:15.060
actual measurements of
the elements of the CKM

00:08:15.060 --> 00:08:17.000
matrix [INAUDIBLE].

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:19.560
And without actually explaining
how we do this experiment,

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:21.923
you can assume that
all measurements have--

00:08:21.923 --> 00:08:23.840
well, you can understand
that all measurements

00:08:23.840 --> 00:08:26.720
have to do with the weak
interaction with quarks.

00:08:26.720 --> 00:08:32.030
That's how we have access
to the CKM matrix elements.

00:08:32.030 --> 00:08:35.906
Sometimes this results in
the modification of masses

00:08:35.906 --> 00:08:38.539
or splitting of mass
states, and sometimes

00:08:38.539 --> 00:08:43.710
the direct measurement
cause a recoupling.

00:08:43.710 --> 00:08:46.050
When you put all of those
measurements back together,

00:08:46.050 --> 00:08:47.600
you can look at this.

00:08:47.600 --> 00:08:51.310
So we see our triangle here.

00:08:51.310 --> 00:08:56.830
We see this point, eta and
rho, which is given here

00:08:56.830 --> 00:08:58.660
in this right-angular plane.

00:08:58.660 --> 00:09:02.860
And you see various number of
measurements which correspond

00:09:02.860 --> 00:09:10.920
to elements of this CKM matrix.

